
  The testing strategy follows from Section 1's main structural decision: because [38;5;153mrules.js[39m is pure, the hard part of
  this feature is testable without clocks, DOM, or storage.

  - [1m[38;5;153mrules.js[39m — table-driven unit tests, where most of the value is.[0m Cases: exactly at [38;5;153mdueAt[39m; exactly at the lead
    boundary; done and unwatched tasks excluded; overdue superseding due-soon on catch-up; dedupe keys stable across a
    simulated reload; a rescheduled task re-arming; tasks with no [38;5;153mdueAt[39m producing nothing.
  - [1mStores — unit tests against a fake storage object[0m, including the corrupt-JSON and quota-exceeded paths, since those
    are the ones that would otherwise take the app down on boot.
